    "preamble": "Wp-8592W-2016 on 17 June, 2016 1 17.06.2016",
    "facts": "In course of hearing it has transpired that the orders impugned in these writ petitions are appellable before a tribunal to be constituted under Section 70 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. The Central Government and the State Government have concurrent powers to constitute tribunals thereunder. Mr. Mehmood Pracha, learned advocate appearing for the Food Safety and Standard Authority as well as Mr. Gupta, learned Additional Advocate General, who has been requested to enter appearance on behalf of the State, are unable to say whether any appellate tribunal has been constituted or not.",
